<title>USA: U.S. attache sees Taiwan corn imports steady.</title>
<headline>U.S. attache sees Taiwan corn imports steady.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. agricultural attache forecast Taiwan corn imports would hold steady as shifts in consumer demands to poultry meat and fish offset an outbreak of foot-and-mouth diease that has devastated the hog industry.</p>
<p>In a report dated April 30 that was released in Washington on Monday, the attache pegged Taiwan total corn imports at 5.1 million tonnes for calendar year 1997 and 5.2 million tonnes for calendar year 1998.</p>
<p>The attache said the United States was expected to continue to supply some 95 percent of imports.</p>
<p>The attache also predicted Taiwan wheat imports would remain stable. Attache reports are not USDA official data.</p>
</text>
